# Explain the hard lines

When writing or editing code in this project, comment the lines a reader cannot understand by glancing at them.

Comment these line by line, in plain language, directly above the line:

- Hardcoded numbers, colors, ids, limits, and sample text. Say what the value is for.
- Regex, route patterns like `/:username`, and template strings that build a link.
- Storage, cloning, and id tricks (`localStorage`, `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...))`, `Date.now()`).
- Conditions that decide what appears on screen (`step === "compose"`, empty checks, owner checks).

```jsx
// 240 characters keeps one whisper short enough for the card.
maxLength={240}
```

Skip a comment when the line is already obvious, such as a closing brace or a label that repeats the text on screen.
